        "maxLength": null,
        "documentation": "When the connection sweep last examined this brain — the **across-users**\ncursor for `lib/app/jobs.ts` (phase 7).\n\n`registerAppJob` fires one process-wide callback while `sweepConnections`\ntakes an `OwnerScope`, so the job has to choose whose brain to sweep.\n\"The first N spaces\" would re-sweep the same N for ever — which is exactly\nthe bug the sweep's own per-type `sweptAt` cursor exists to prevent,\nreappearing one level up and just as silently. Ordering by this column\n(nulls first) and stamping as it goes makes the rotation cover everyone.\n\nNullable and unset means \"never swept\", which sorts first: a brand-new\nbrain is picked up on the next tick rather than after everyone else."
